Licensing issues inherited from WebFormsForCore
-----------------------------------------------

These came with the fork base and are not covered by the licences above (docs/LICENSING.md has the details):

  * Resolved: the .NET Framework webengine.dll/webengine4.dll binaries and the decompiled Microsoft Report Viewer
    were removed; the decompiled Microsoft.Web.Infrastructure and System.Security.Cryptography.DataProtector were
    rewritten by webForCore from their documented APIs (MIT); the decompiled System.Web.RegularExpressions classes are
    compiled only for .NET Framework.
  * Open: about 140 files in src/WebFormsForCore.Configuration (settings, System.Net.Configuration, the config XML
    classes, configuration builders) were decompiled from .NET Framework assemblies. Their originals are MIT-licensed
    (Reference Source, dotnet/runtime) and are to replace them.
  * The machine.config and web.config files in src/WebFormsForCore.Configuration/Config come from a .NET Framework
    installation.
  * Sample assets in src/BundleTransformer/samples (not built) include the Blogger Sans font (CC BY-ND 4.0), the
    Bitstream Vera font, a jquery.validate-vsdoc.js under Microsoft's ASP.NET MVC 3 licence terms, and images of
    unknown origin.
